-->|notes=<li>Damage stacks up to 6 times, not 5, though the Slow stacks up to 5 times.<li>Basic Attacks deal a tick of damage per new stack and refresh the duration of all stacks. They also restart the DoT tick timer for each stack, synchronizing them (so the next damage tick for all stacks will be 0.5s after the most recent Basic Attack).<li>This also means DoT ticks that happen on the same server tick (1/16 s) as a Basic Attack generally happen twice (the DoT takes place and then the on-hit DoT tick from the Basic Attack resolves) There is observed to be about a 75% chance of this happening when a Basic Attack resolves, and a 25% chance of only 1 tick per stack, for reasons not fully understood. This is hypothesized to be because the Basic Attack, which applies and refreshes DoT durations, and the pre-scheduled DoT ticks happen on the same server tick, so which resolves first is seemingly random.}};File:Burn_Notice_Icon.png;
